    "PackageLink",
    BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"], "[", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["g", "TI"], ",", " ", 
    StyleBox["r", "TI"], ",", " ", 
    StyleBox["target", "TI"]}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4cb5d72e-884c-4e9b-a441-54d54d48aa07"],
 "\[LineSeparator]",
 "gives the minimum number needed to cover the vertices of ",
 StyleBox["target", "TI"],
 ", using centres anywhere in ",
 StyleBox["g", "TI"],
 "."
}], "Usage",ExpressionUUID->"4a54488d-07a5-4de7-b08e-80993b084edc"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The covering number is the minimum size of a centre set whose closed \
radius-",
 StyleBox["r", "TI"],
 " balls cover the target. For the whole graph this is the ",
 StyleBox["r", "TI"],
 "-domination number, and at radius one the domination number. The graph is \
finite, undirected and unweighted; the radius is a nonnegative integer, \
defaulting to 1. The target defaults to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["All"]], "paclet:ref/All"},
   "RefLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "5d1810aa-4910-48d2-83fb-75794cc7a2dd"],
 "."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"beb9c7da-a635-48b2-a1b3-60b7fe6ab91d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Targets can be vertices, vertex lists, density associations, graph carriers \
or abstract regions such as ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["InfraBall"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraBall", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "75b50d7e-a1c7-48c4-a9aa-d388061ef519"],
 ". Only vertex support matters. A literal vertex takes precedence over list \
interpretation. All centres and shortest paths belong to the ambient graph."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"b1d1a208-4157-411b-ae2a-2b9296c51c5d"],

